eading into the back end of July.\n\nThe structure story on the daily timeframe is one of gradual accumulation following a decisive push higher on 14\u201315 July, when the pair broke out of its consolidation range and printed a high of 0.7021. That move established the 0.7000\u20130.7021 area as a zone of prior reaction, and the subsequent behaviour has been telling: price has repeatedly tested the round number from below and above without committing in either direction, suggesting the market is in a digestion phase rather than a reversal. The four-touch support at 0.6961 provides a meaningful floor beneath current levels, while the 0.6884 prior reaction zone offers a deeper structural reference should conditions deteriorate more significantly. To the topside, the 0.7184 prior reaction zone remains a longer-range reference, though the more immediate structural resistance sits at 0.6989, a level that has attracted selling interest on at least two occasions and which price is currently pressing against.\n\nThe H1 picture reinforces the cautious near-term tone. After spending much of yesterday's European and US session trading comfortably above 0.7000, the pair slipped back through that level during the overnight Asian session, with the 00:00 candle marking the initial break and subsequent hours consolidating in the 0.6986\u20130.6994 range. The most recent H1 candles show a modest drift lower towards 0.6982, with the session low touching 0.6982 itself. The 0.6989 structure resistance is now acting as a ceiling on an hourly basis, and until price reclaims that level with conviction, the intraday read is one of consolidation rather than continuation.\n\nThe calendar is empty for today's session, which removes the prospect of scheduled macro catalysts driving a sharp directional move. In the absence of event risk, price action is likely to remain technically driven, with liquidity conditions potentially thinner than usual. That environment can amplify moves in either direction if a significant order flow imbalance emerges, but it equally supports range-bound behaviour around the current zone.\n\nThe bullish read would come under pressure on a daily close beneath the 0.6961 prior reaction zone, which would represent a break of the higher-low structure built since late June. A sustained move back into the 0.6884 support area would materially alter the near-term thesis. Conversely, a clean hourly close above 0.6989 and a recapture of 0.7000 on a closing basis would suggest the digestion phase is resolving in favour of the prevailing trend.\n\nThis is editorial analysis, not financial advice. Trading involves substantial risk of loss.", "sample": false}